## 4. Designation
**Definition:**  
A formal legal or protected status assigned by a federal, state, county, or local authority.

**Rules:**  
Use only approved Designations.

### Controlled Vocabulary: Designation

#### A. Federal Designations
National Park  
National Monument  
National Historic Site  
National Memorial  
National Historic Landmark  
National Natural Landmark  
National Recreation Area  
National Wildlife Refuge  
National Scenic Trail  
National Heritage Area  
National Battlefield  
National Cemetery  
National Register of Historic Places (NRHP)  

#### B. State Designations
State Park  
State Nature Preserve  
State Fishing Area  
State Hunting Area  
State Memorial  
State Wildlife Area  
State Forest  
State Scenic River  
State Natural Landmark  
State Archaeological Preserve  
State Historic Site  
State Recreation Area  

#### C. Local / Special Designations
County Nature Preserve  
County Historic Landmark  
Municipal Historic Landmark  
Local Landmark  
Local Historic District  
Certified Arboretum (Level I–IV)  
Registered Cemetery  
Protected Wetland  
Mitigation Bank  
Conservation Easement  
Land Trust Preserve  

#### D. Blank (no designation)
Most sites will have no formal designation.

---

## 5. Ownership
**Definition:**  
The legal owner of the land.

**Rules:**  
- Use the official agency or organization name.  
- Do not infer ownership.

---

## 6. Management
**Definition:**  
The entity responsible for operating or stewarding the site.

**Rules:**  
- Use the official managing agency.  
- Semicolon‑delimit multiple managers.  
- If same as Ownership, repeat explicitly.

---

## 7. Coordination
**Definition:**  
Entities that coordinate but do not own or manage the site.

**Rules:**  
- Use only when coordination is formally recognized.  
- Leave blank if none.

---

## 8. Description
**Definition:**  
A concise, factual summary of the site’s identity, purpose, and landscape or ecological character.

**Rules:**  
- 1–3 sentences.  
- Include identity‑defining ecological characteristics.  
- Include essential governance or naming history.  
- Include former names and synonyms.  
- No amenities.  
- No temporary conditions.

---

## 9. Status
**Allowed Values:**  
Active  
Seasonal  
Access Permit Required  
No Public Entry  
Under Development  
Proposed  
Abandoned  
Closed  

**Rules:**  
- “Closed” = permanently closed as the entity described.  
- “Proposed” must be officially referenced.

---

## 10. Address
Leave blank if no formal address exists.

---

## 11. Acres
Numeric only.  
Leave blank if unknown.

---

## 12. Location
Municipality or township only.  
Semicolon‑delimit if multiple.  
Do not include county names.

---

## 13. County
List all counties the site spans.  
Alphabetical.  
Semicolon‑delimited.  
Do not include the word “County.”

---

## 14. GPS Coordinates
Format: `lat,lon`  
One coordinate pair only.  
No space after comma.

---

## 15. Plus Code
Generated from accepted coordinates.  
Blank if GPS is blank.

---

